# Design tokens

App UI must use **semantic** color tokens (`bg`, `fg`, `bg.photo`, `accent.solid`, …). Do not put raw hex, `rgb()`, `rgba()`, `hsl()`, `oklch()`, or primitive palette steps (`ink.950`, `teal.500`) in component props, `style={{}}`, or local constants.

Tokens live in `src/design-system/tokens/` (primitives) and `src/design-system/theme/semantic-tokens.ts` (roles). ESLint fails the build on hardcoded hex in `src/`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Box bg="#0B0F14" />
<Box bg="ink.950" color="white" />

// ✅ GOOD — semantic, theme-aware product chrome
<Box bg="bg" color="fg" />

// ✅ GOOD — semantic, photographic surfaces (same in light and dark)
<Box bg="bg.photo" color="fg.photo" />
```

If the role you need is missing, add a semantic token in `semantic-tokens.ts` that points at a primitive. Do not invent a one-off hex or use `ink.*` in a screen.

Do not use Chakra's unthemed palettes (`gray`, `red`, `orange`, `whiteAlpha`, …). Use `teal` (the one primary), `danger`/`caution`/`success` for status, `lime` only for wind data.
